 r←RunTest(test mode folder);ok;start;status;msg;detail;dm;stack
⍝ Run one test function (mode is 'watcher': mocked when USE_MOCK_FSW) and report how it went
⍝ r ← status message detail milliseconds folder, where status is 'passed', 'failed' (an assertion failed) or 'error' (any other error),
⍝ detail is a vector of lines saying where it went wrong (the error as the interpreter displays it and the stack, see RecordError)
⍝ and folder is the one the next test should use (Recover may have had to switch to a fresh one)
⍝ Assertion failures signal ASSERT_EN (see AssertFailed) and are trapped here so that Run can carry on with the next test
⍝ When debugging (⎕SE.Link.DEBUG≠0) nothing is trapped, so that a failing test stops where it went wrong
 :If USE_MOCK_FSW ⋄ ⎕SE.Link.Watcher.(CRAWLER MOCK)←0 1 ⍝ mocked watcher: links watch, but no watcher is started - DOTNET stays as detected
 :Else ⋄ ⎕SE.Link.Watcher.(CRAWLER MOCK)←0 0 ⍝ a real FileSystemWatcher (never the crawler)
 :EndIf
 ASSERT_FAILURES←0⍴⊂''
 detail←0⍴⊂''
 start←3⊃⎕AI
 :If ×⎕SE.Link.DEBUG
     ok←(⍎test)folder NAME
 :Else
     :Trap 0
         ok←CallTest test folder ⍝ records the stack in LAST_ERROR before this :Trap cuts it back
     :Case ASSERT_EN
         (status msg)←'failed'(⎕DMX.Message)
         (dm stack)←LAST_ERROR
         detail←(⊂'ASSERTION FAILED: ',msg),(0<≢stack)/(⊂'Stack:'),'  '∘,¨stack
     :Else
         (dm stack)←LAST_ERROR
         :If 0=≢dm ⋄ dm←⎕DMX.DM ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ RecordError did not get to run
         (status msg)←'error'(⎕DMX.(EM,(×≢Message)/': ',Message),' ⍝ at ',2⊃dm)
         detail←(⊂msg),(1↓dm),(0<≢stack)/(⊂'Stack:'),'  '∘,¨stack ⍝ the offending line and the caret under it, as the interpreter shows them
         :If 0≠≢ASSERT_FAILURES ⋄ msg,←' ⋄ after failed assertions: ',⊃{⍺,' ⋄ ',⍵}/ASSERT_FAILURES ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ recorded when ASSERT_ERROR=0
     :EndTrap
 :EndIf
 :If 0=⎕NC'status' ⍝ the test ran to completion
     :If 0≠≢ASSERT_FAILURES ⋄ (status msg)←'failed'(⊃{⍺,' ⋄ ',⍵}/ASSERT_FAILURES)
     :ElseIf ok≢1 ⋄ (status msg)←'failed'('test returned ',⍕ok)
     :Else ⋄ (status msg)←'passed' ''
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
 :If status≢'passed' ⋄ folder←Recover folder ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ the test will not have cleaned up after itself
 r←status msg detail((3⊃⎕AI)-start)folder
